      "unit": 15,
      "title": {"ar": "إلسَّاعَة", "en": "The Hour"},
      "pages": [24, 25],
      "continues": false,
      "incomplete": false,
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "grammar",
          "src": "p.24",
          "topic": "Telling the time",
          "note": "Explanation: 1. In Arabic, the word ساعة (hour) is used to express time. To express 1:00 and 2:00, use the feminine form of the numbers. 2. Use these words to express the time: و = and, followed by the number of minutes after the hour; إلّا = less/minus, followed by the number of minutes before the hour; نُصّ = half (half an hour); رُبع = quarter (quarter of an hour); ثُلْث = third (20 minutes) (You can also say تِلْت or ثِلِث).",
          "examples": [
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة وَحدِة.", "en": "It's one o'clock (the hour is one)."},
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة ثِنْتين.", "en": "It's two o'clock (the hour is two)."},
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة ثمانية.", "en": "It's eight o'clock (the hour is eight)."},
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة سَبْعة ورُبع.", "en": "It's a quarter after seven (seven and a quarter)."},
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة سَبْعة وثِلِث.", "en": "It's twenty after seven (seven and a third)."},
            {"ar": "إلسّاعة سَبْعة إلّا ثُلْث.", "en": "It's twenty to seven (seven minus a third)."}
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "grammar",
          "src": "p.25",
          "topic": "a.m. / p.m.",
          "note": "3. To express the part of the day (a.m. or p.m.), say the time and then add a time expression such as \"[in] the morning\" or \"[in] the afternoon.\"",
          "examples": [
            {"ar": "الساعة خَمْسِة الصُّبح.", "en": "It's five in the morning."},
            {"ar": "الساعة ثلاثِة بَعْدِ الظُّهُر.", "en": "It's three in the afternoon."}
          ]
        },
        {
